            <ArticleTitle>A rare cause of sciatica discovered during digital rectal examination: case report of an intrapelvic sciatic notch schwannoma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1080/02688697.2017.1378801</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Intrapelvic sciatic nerve schwannomas are rare causes for non-discogenic sciatica. We describe a 44-year-old female who had a palpable mass on digital rectal examination that exhibited a positive Tinel's sign. The schwannoma was excised by a posterior transgluteal approach. Patients with negative spinal imaging should undergo pelvic scanning to rule out these tumors.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
